          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انطباع (inṭibāʿ) is built on the native Arabic root ṭ-b-ʿ, \"to stamp, to imprint\" (Lane). Inṭibāʿ is the Form VII verbal noun, being stamped: the mark a thing leaves on the mind, an impression."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
