          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "منظور (manẓūr) is built on the native Arabic root n-ẓ-r, \"to look, to regard\" (Lane). Manẓūr is the passive participle, what is looked at; in modern use it is the angle you look from."
            }
          ]
        },
